<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><fdroid><repo icon="icon.png" name="restoid (DEPRECATED)" pubkey="" timestamp="1795847574" url="https://hddq.github.io/restoid/fdroid/repo" version="20002"><description>⚠️ DEPRECATED: This repository is deprecated. Please migrate to the central F-Droid repository at https://fdroid.hddq.org/repo</description></repo><application id="io.github.hddq.restoid"><id>io.github.hddq.restoid</id><added>2026-11-28</added><lastupdated>2026-11-28</lastupdated><name>Restoid - Backup Tool</name><summary>Secure, deduplicated backup for apps and files powered by the restic engine.</summary><desc>Restoid is a modern, privacy-focused backup solution for Android powered by the robust, open-source restic engine. Keep your apps, data, contacts, call logs, photos, and documents safe with enterprise-grade encryption and lightning-fast, space-saving deduplication.

Whether you want to back up photos to a home NAS, store encrypted snapshots in the cloud, or preserve full app data on a rooted device, Restoid gives you complete control without trackers, ads, or proprietary lock-in.

Root access is completely optional: back up custom folders, photos, documents, contacts, and call logs without root; root access is only needed to back up private app data.

Key Features:

Blazing Fast &amp; Deduplicated
• Content-Defined Deduplication: Only unique changed blocks are uploaded, making subsequent backups blazingly fast and drastically more efficient than traditional tar.gz archives.
• Space-Saving: Multiple snapshots share common data, keeping storage footprints minimal.

Zero-Knowledge Encryption
• Enterprise security: All snapshots are encrypted with restic using state-of-the-art cryptography.
• Your passwords and encryption keys remain entirely under your control.

Flexible Storage Backends
• Local Storage: Save to internal memory, SD card, or USB OTG drives.
• Native Network Backends: Direct support for SFTP (SSH key &amp; password), REST server, and Amazon S3-compatible object storage (Garage, MinIO, Wasabi, Cloudflare R2, Backblaze B2).
• Cloud &amp; Extra Backends via Rclone: Connect to dozens of storage providers and protocols (such as Google Drive, OneDrive, Dropbox, WebDAV, Nextcloud, pCloud, and more) with built-in rclone support by importing or pasting an rclone.conf.

Full App &amp; Data Backup (Root Required)
• Selectively back up installed user applications.
• Granular control: Choose whether to include APKs, app data, device-protected data, external files, or OBB caches, and exclude specific paths inside app data (such as large caches or re-downloadable media) while preserving core databases and settings.

Custom Files &amp; Media
• Back up personal folders: DCIM, Documents, Downloads, or any directory on your device.

Contacts &amp; Call Logs
• Back up and restore your contacts (including groups and photos) and call logs without requiring root; backups can run manually or on automated schedules.

Automated Background Schedules
• Configure recurring schedules (daily, weekly, or custom intervals).
• Smart trigger constraints: Run only while charging, on unmetered Wi-Fi, or when battery conditions are met.

Surgical &amp; Safe Restore
• Restore entire apps or specific parts (e.g. restore data without overwriting the installed APK), custom directories, contacts, and call logs.
• Downgrade protection prevents accidental restoration of older versions over newer ones.

Zero Vendor Lock-in
• Standard restic format: Repositories use the native, open-source restic format. You can always access, inspect, mount, or restore your data on any PC (Linux, macOS, Windows) using the official restic CLI—even without your phone.

Maintenance &amp; Repository Health
• Keep your repository compact with automated snapshot retention policies (prune old backups by day, week, month).
• Run repository integrity checks and clear stale locks with one tap.

Modern Material 3 Expressive UI
• Built with modern Jetpack Compose and Material 3 Expressive design, featuring dynamic theming, smooth animations, and edge-to-edge layout.
• 100% Free and Open Source (GPLv3), with zero analytics, telemetry, or third-party tracking.</desc><license>GPL-3.0-only</license><categories>System</categories><category>System</category><web></web><source>https://github.com/hddq/restoid</source><tracker>https://github.com/hddq/restoid/issues</tracker><author>hddq</author><marketversion>0.10.0</marketversion><marketvercode>342</marketvercode><package><version>0.10.0</version><versioncode>342</versioncode><apkname>app-x86_64-release-v0.10.0.apk</apkname><hash type="sha256">c34e2a0df8f4a9322d2eda71472e34b526d1bd55240d606e9ffdc0a68f722d7f</hash><size>60644718</size><sdkver>29</sdkver><targetSdkVersion>37</targetSdkVersion><added>2026-11-28</added><sig>f13c464420c712e65cc683706bcc6738</sig><permissions>ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK,ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE,ACCESS_WIFI_STATE,FOREGROUND_SERVICE,FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC,INTERNET,MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE,POST_NOTIFICATIONS,POST_PROMOTED_NOTIFICATIONS,QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES,READ_CALENDAR,READ_CALL_LOG,READ_CONTACTS,READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE,RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED,REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS,USE_BIOMETRIC,USE_FINGERPRINT,WAKE_LOCK,WRITE_CALENDAR,WRITE_CALL_LOG,WRITE_CONTACTS,WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE,io.github.hddq.restoid.DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION</permissions><uses-permission maxSdkVersion="29" name="android.permission.READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE"/><uses-permission maxSdkVersion="29" name="android.permission.WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE"/><nativecode>x86_64</nativecode></package><package><version>0.10.0</version><versioncode>341</versioncode><apkname>app-arm64-v8a-release-v0.10.0.apk</apkname><hash type="sha256">74dbb1e53c1e14a913663f09d9a09d0be6478a9a8ff8ef1451ed8b57613636f0</hash><size>48521162</size><sdkver>29</sdkver><targetSdkVersion>37</targetSdkVersion><added>2026-11-28</added><sig>f13c464420c712e65cc683706bcc6738</sig><permissions>ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK,ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE,ACCESS_WIFI_STATE,FOREGROUND_SERVICE,FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC,INTERNET,MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE,POS